                <pb facs="0480" n="386" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg386"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Smythe.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 169.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to your No. 191, of March 2 last,
                    and to your No. 204, of April 30, 1896, relative to the expulsion of Hugo O.
                    Loewi from Haiti, I have to say that the promise of the minister for foreign
                    affairs, made in your No. 191, to furnish you with a statement in writing giving
                    the reasons for Mr. Loewi’s expulsion, has never been fulfilled.</p>
                <p>You are accordingly instructed to request that the promised statement be promptly
                    furnished you for submission to your Government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
